Self-adhesive plastic labels fall under heading 3919 (self-adhesive plates, sheets, film, foil, tape, strip and other flat shapes, of plastics) unless they are printed and classified in Chapter 49. Under heading 4911, printed labels are generally excluded for plastic labels: Chapter 49 covers printed matter, and the printing must be more than incidental to the primary use. Here the printing is the essential purpose, since the label conveys battery polarity direction information. Printed self-adhesive plastic labels are, however, commonly classified under 3919 when the printing is incidental, and under 4911.99 when the printing is the primary purpose. Note 2 to Chapter 39 excludes printed goods of Chapter 49, and CBP has ruled that plastic labels printed with information are 4911.99.

Within 4911.99, the subdivisions are 4911.99.20 (printed labels, tags... ?). Actually, the 4911.99 subheadings are 4911.99.2000 (Printed charts, graphs, and similar... for educational?), 4911.99.4000 (Printed...), 4911.99.60 (Printed...), 4911.99.80 (Other). The "Other" subheading is 4911.99.8000 with statistical suffixes, and 4911.99.8000 is the general "Other" provision. 

{"hts_code": "4911.99.8000", "reason": "A self-adhesive plastic label whose essential purpose is the printed battery-direction information is classified as other printed matter in heading 4911 (Chapter 39 Note 2 excludes it from 3919)."}
